#: ../../../release/dev/pch-warnings.rst:2
msgid "pch-warnings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/dev/pch-warnings.rst:4
msgid ""
"The :prop_tgt:`PCH_WARNINGS` target property, and its initializing :variable:"
"`CMAKE_PCH_WARNINGS` variable, were added to enable compiler warnings for "
"the headers collected into a precompiled header.  Previously the generated "
"precompiled header was always marked as a system header, which suppressed "
"those warnings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/dev/pch-warnings.rst:10
msgid ""
"The system header marker now comes from an internal "
"``CMAKE_PCH_SYSTEM_HEADER_PRAGMA`` variable instead of from "
"``CMAKE_PCH_PROLOGUE``.  Projects that cleared or replaced "
"``CMAKE_PCH_PROLOGUE`` in order to drop the marker no longer affect it, and "
"must set :prop_tgt:`PCH_WARNINGS` or :variable:`CMAKE_PCH_WARNINGS` instead."
msgstr ""
